        "event": "Special Weather Statement",
        "headline": "Special Weather Statement issued August 29 at 7:38PM AKDT by NWS Anchorage AK",
        "description": "Strong northwesterly winds have developed across Shelikof Strait\nand the waters around southern Kodiak Island. These winds are\nresuspending ash from the 1912 Katmai-Novarupta eruption,\npotentially causing haze and trace amounts of ash accumulation.\nThe villages of Karluk and Larsen Bay are most likely to be\nimpacted.\n\nThose in sensitive groups or with respiratory ailments are\nencouraged to avoid or reduce outdoor activity to avoid inhaling\nthe ash. The winds will weaken slowly through the day Su",
